From 5f02c814fdeed7b89abb8193a7f2c2baa7baf77d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 00:30:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 145/188] PCI/ASPM: force L1 support on MSI Claw 8 EX AI+
 RTS5264 root port
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The MSI Claw 8 EX AI+ BIOS E1T91IMS.105 advertises only ASPM L0s in the
Link Capabilities of the PCH PCIe root port (8086:e43a) that hosts the
RTS5264 SD card reader, even though the port supports ASPM L1 and L1 PM
substates. Because the ASPM core therefore leaves aspm_l1_support clear,
it never programs L1/L1SS on the link, the port's PMC power-gate domain
never gates, and the SoC can never reach S0ix during s2idle.

The port's read-only capability registers are self-inconsistent. Its
Link Capabilities register (CAP_EXP+0x0c) reads 0x03736413, ASPM
Support = L0s only, while its L1 PM Substates capability (0x204) reads
0x00293c3f, advertising ASPM L1.1 and L1.2 as supported. The downstream
RTS5264 advertises ASPM L1 in its own Link Capabilities, so only the
root port under-reports.

Add a DMI-gated header fixup that marks the root port L1-capable so the
ASPM core programs the L1.2 timing on the link.

Holo: this one should likely be fixed in the BIOS by MSI/Intel.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Nícolas F. R. A. Prado <nfraprado@collabora.com>
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index a6d33bc24..cf406ff35 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -6548,3 +6548,28 @@ static void quirk_rts5264_reset_degraded_link(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 }
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_REALTEK, 0x5264,
 			quirk_rts5264_reset_degraded_link);
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_PCIEASPM
+/*
+ * MSI Claw 8 EX AI+ (MS-1T91): the BIOS hides ASPM L1 from the Link
+ * Capabilities of the Root Port hosting the RTS5264 reader, so the
+ * ASPM core never programs L1/L1SS, the PMC power-gate domain never
+ * gates, and the SoC cannot reach S0ix in s2idle. Mark the Port
+ * L1-capable.
+ */
+static void quirk_msi_claw8_rp_aspm_l1(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	if (dev->devfn != PCI_DEVFN(0x1c, 0))
+		return;
+
+	if (!dmi_match(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "MS-1T91"))
+		return;
+
+	if (dev->aspm_l1_support)
+		return;
+
+	dev->aspm_l1_support = 1;
+	pci_info(dev, "ASPM: forcing L1 support (MSI Claw 8 EX AI+ hides L1 in LnkCap)\n");
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0xe43a, quirk_msi_claw8_rp_aspm_l1);
+#endif
